** shallow two-bar (von Mises) truss of finite strain trusses (Neo-Hooke), pushed through its snap-through by
** displacement control of the apex; the supports are tied by a quadratic truss; tests the co-rotated finite strain truss formulation
*material, name=compressibleneohooke, id=rubber, provider=marmot
3000.0, 1000.0, 1e-9

*node
1, 0.0, 0.0
2, 10.0, 1.0
3, 20.0, 0.0
4, 10.0, 0.0

*element, type=T2D2CR
1, 1, 2
2, 2, 3

*element, type=T2D3CR
3, 1, 3, 4

*elSet, elSet=bars
1, 2

*elSet, elSet=tie
3

*nSet, nSet=supports
1, 3
*nSet, nSet=apex
2
*nSet, nSet=tieMid
4

*section, name=barSection, area=1.0, material=rubber, type=truss
bars

*section, name=tieSection, area=0.2, material=rubber, type=truss
tie

*job, name=job, domain=2d
*solver, solver=NIST, name=theSolver

*fieldOutput
>>perNode, name=displacement, elSet=all, field=displacement, result=U
>>perElement, name=normalForce, elSet=all, result=normal force, quadraturePoint=0,
>>perNode, name=F, nSet=apex, field=displacement, result=P, f(x)='sum(x[:,1])', saveHistory=True,
>>perElement, name=N, elSet=bars, result=normal force, quadraturePoint=0, saveHistory=True,

*output, type=ensight, name=esExport
>>perNode, fieldOutput=displacement
>>perElement, fieldOutput=normalForce
>>configuration, overwrite=yes

*step, solver=theSolver
maxInc=0.05, minInc=1e-8, maxNumInc=1000, maxIter=15, stepLength=1
>>initializematerial, name=init, elSet=all
>>dirichlet, name=supports, nSet=supports, field=displacement, 2=0
>>dirichlet, name=tieMid, nSet=tieMid, field=displacement, 2=0
>>dirichlet, name=apex, nSet=apex, field=displacement, 1=0, 2=-2.0
